    <briefdescription>
<para>Type, format, and encoding errors. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classcslt_1_1FormatError" kindref="compound">FormatError</ref> represents errors related to type mismatches, invalid data formats, encoding issues, parsing failures, and validation errors.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example Usage:</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Using<sp/>default<sp/>message</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>FormatError();<sp/><sp/>//<sp/>&quot;Format<sp/>error&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Using<sp/>custom<sp/>message</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>FormatError(&quot;Invalid<sp/>JSON<sp/>format<sp/>at<sp/>line<sp/>42&quot;);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
